\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Squares of differences}
\date{2026-11-03}


\p{A lattice field action sums squares of differences,
##{\sum_e\bigl(\varphi(h(e))-\varphi(s(e))\bigr)^2,}
the discrete form of #{\int|\nabla\varphi|^2}. A pairing sums products
of the values themselves, the discrete form of #{\int fg} when each
site has unit volume. Both expressions need coefficients that can be
squared and added, and a sum of squares that vanishes only when every
term does. The next definition specializes the earlier difference to
real numbers and writes those sums.}
